1
00:00:01,626 --> 00:00:09,182
Getting started
How to find your way around the CRM before you work in any module.

2
00:00:09,198 --> 00:00:13,455
Sign in as Priya Ramdin — Relationship Manager
Relationship manager — her own book of clients and enquiries

3
00:00:13,455 --> 00:00:16,155
Your home page opens on the dashboard for your role
Relationship managers land on My Workbench

4
00:00:16,155 --> 00:00:19,983
At the top: the Service Levels radiator
Your items that are breached, at risk or on track — click one to open it

5
00:00:19,983 --> 00:00:25,192
Below it: My Workbench — open enquiries, next-best actions, reviews and KYC
Every widget only counts records you are allowed to see

6
00:00:25,192 --> 00:00:29,389
Switch to any other dashboard you may see from this menu
Group Executive, Lead Funnel, Lending Pipeline, Wealth…

7
00:00:29,389 --> 00:00:35,491
The sidebar groups the modules by business area
Tools · Documents · Client 360 · Lending · Investments · Advisory · Growth · Service · Compliance · Masters

8
00:00:35,491 --> 00:00:38,734
You only see the modules your role is allowed to use
An RM sees client, lending, investment and service modules — not the advisory deal room

9
00:00:38,734 --> 00:00:44,479
Search finds clients, enquiries, applications and more
By name, number, email or phone — results respect what you may see

10
00:00:44,479 --> 00:00:46,664
Pick a result to open it
Here: the client Deepak Seegoolam — the client record comes first

11
00:00:46,664 --> 00:00:50,102
Open a module, then pick an object from the tabs at the top
Enquiries & Leads ▸ Enquiries

12
00:00:50,102 --> 00:00:54,798
The Table view: sort by a column, filter, search, select rows for bulk actions
Export gives a CSV of what you see

13
00:00:54,798 --> 00:01:00,228
The Pipeline view: a Kanban board with one column per stage
Drag a card to another column to move it — gates may ask for missing information first

14
00:01:00,228 --> 00:01:04,854
Click a record to open its panel
Header with stage and actions · fields grouped by heading · tabs underneath

15
00:01:04,854 --> 00:01:07,558
Calculated fields are greyed and update by themselves
Lead score and grade, indicative rate and instalment

16
00:01:07,558 --> 00:01:11,767
Related: every record linked to this one
For a client: applications, KYC cases, mandates, holdings, requests…

17
00:01:11,767 --> 00:01:15,704
Activity: calls, meetings, emails and notes
Log your own call or note here

18
00:01:15,704 --> 00:01:19,841
Tasks: follow-ups with an owner, due date and priority
Overdue tasks appear on your workbench

19
00:01:19,841 --> 00:01:24,053
Docs: documents, the document checklist, upload, share and e-signature
Ask the client for documents with a secure upload link

20
00:01:24,053 --> 00:01:28,203
Audit: who changed what and when
Stage changes, approvals with comments and data reveals

21
00:01:28,203 --> 00:01:35,474
Add a follow-up task on the record
Tasks tab ▸ new task

22
00:01:35,474 --> 00:01:38,181
The task is saved on the record and appears on your workbench

23
00:01:38,181 --> 00:01:42,031
The bell shows new assignments, approvals waiting for you and SLA warnings
Click a notification to open the record or approval

24
00:01:42,031 --> 00:01:47,765
Approvals: credit decisions, KYC sign-off and maker-checker steps wait here
Tools ▸ Approvals — the person who asked can never approve their own request

25
00:01:47,765 --> 00:01:52,967
My Reminders: personal nudges you can snooze or complete
Tools ▸ My Reminders

26
00:01:52,967 --> 00:02:02,830
Personalise: light or dark mode, text size and motion
The palette icon in the header

27
00:02:02,830 --> 00:02:14,643
EN | FR switches module, field, stage and picklist names to French
Useful when working with French-speaking clients

28
00:02:14,643 --> 00:02:18,390
Sign out from the header when you are done
Avatar ▸ Security: change password, two-factor authentication, calendar feed

29
00:02:18,390 --> 00:02:23,800
Pick a module tutorial
Each module has its own end-to-end video in this folder.
